==English==
[[File:Cetorhinus maximus by greg skomal.JPG|thumb|A basking shark]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-basking shark.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A very large [[shark]], {{taxlink|Cetorhinus maximus|species}}, that feeds at or close to the surface by filtering [[plankton]] from the water and is found in all the world's temperate oceans.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Book of Sharks| author={{w|Richard Ellis (biologist) |Richard Ellis}}| year=1983| publisher=Knopf|ISBN=0679722106|passage=Like the whale shark, the '''basking shark''' is a huge, slow-moving plankton feeder. Also like the whale shark, the '''basking shark''' is the sole member of a family created especially to accommodate it.|page=89}}

